Subject: [PATCH 52/59] fix(gauntlet-tdd): correct three defects self-review
 found in the loop (gcp-dnxq)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three bugs, all of the same family: each is silent at the default and only
bites a caller who sets `contracts_dir`, which is exactly the caller no test
run exercises unless it is written to.

1. `gauntlet lint` was passed `--contracts-dir <path>`. It does not take that
   flag — verified against the CLI, not the help text: `lint: unknown flag:
   --contracts-dir`. `gauntlet lint [path]` takes a POSITIONAL path while
   `gauntlet run local` takes the flag, so the two spellings are derived
   separately now (LINT_ARGS / RUN_ARGS) from one `contracts_dir` value.

2. The red gate parsed its finding count out of stderr. `gauntlet lint --json`
   writes the whole report to STDOUT and leaves stderr empty, so the parse
   always yielded nothing and `red_findings:` was recorded as `unparsed` on
   every run. Now `jq -r '.findings // [] | length'` against the JSON, with
   the real shape documented in the step (`findings` is null when clean, an
   array of {path,line,kind,message} when not).

3. `$CONTRACTS_FLAG` and `$CONTRACT_PATH` were set in one step and read in
   later ones. A formula step is a separate agent turn and the routed
   `implement` step is a separate SESSION, so neither survives. The failure is
   not a crash: an empty `$LINT_ARGS` reads as "gauntlet's default .gauntlet",
   so the later gates would address a different tree than the one scaffolded
   into and still report success. Values that must cross a boundary now go
   through the root bead's notes (`implement` reads `contract_path:` back);
   everything else is re-derived from the `{{contracts_dir}}` token, which
   does render in every step.

Two new guards so none of it recurs, both mutation-checked:

- CliSurfaceTests: no `gauntlet lint` invocation may pass `--contracts-dir`.
- NoCrossStepShellStateTests: every `$VAR` a step reads must be assigned in
  that same step's shell blocks (ambient GC_*/BEADS_*/HOME-style names
  excepted). Deleting the green gate's own derivation turns it red.

The shell-block extractor now strips trailing `#` comments before scanning,
outside double-quoted spans. Without that, the explanatory
`# gauntlet run local --contracts-dir <path>` comment beside RUN_ARGS read as
an unpinned `run local` invocation and tripped the lane-pin guard — a comment
naming a command is documentation, not a run.

Verified by executing the corrected snippets against the real CLI with
`contracts_dir` set — the case that was broken: red gate exit 1 with
RED_FINDINGS=1 and the finding rendered; green gate lint=0 run=0 SKIPPED=0
with `total=3 pass=3 fail=0`. Suite: 19 passed, 41 subtests.
